e counter with `cli.py set-iterations --root . --id 0006 --count 0`, then re-run `/sdlc-deploy 0006`. The next run should apply the saved diff, which the reviewer has not seen yet, and review it.\n- The other two Important findings were added by the framework's automatic checks, and you need to look at them:\n  - **`tests/test_detect_cli.py` edited in a fix-type change.** This edit was declared in the spec (panel decision 1), and you applied `sdlc:unlock-tests` for it. You decide whether that's acceptable.\n  - **`tests/fixtures/sample-python-project/.env` flagged as modified.** I believe this comes from the sandbox masking the file: git can't even read it, and nothing about it is committed. It should be gone in a run outside the sandbox.\n- Nit worth fixing: `docs/OPERATING_MODEL.md:98` still says the runbook Go only checks that a person applied the label; it now requires your account.\n\n**Checks:** I didn't run the full build, test and lint targets, because this run committed only markdown and YAML, no code. In this sandbox, any test that copies the fixture project errors on a \"Permission denied\" reading its `.env` file. With the proposed fix applied, the case-list test passed, the eval's owner-check command passed, and its pytest command found the framework but failed only on that `.env` error. Nothing was merged or deployed.",
