Check results**\n- Build: `python -m compileall -q plugin tests tasks.py .github/scripts` printed nothing.\n- Tests: `tests/test_detect_cli.py` plus `tests/test_owner_rounds.py` gave **1 failed, 121 passed**. The one failure is line 859. Both cases of `test_go_reads_the_owner_from_the_default_branch` and every existing Go test pass.\n- Lint: `ruff check .` printed `All checks passed!`. `ruff format --check .` reported `299 files already formatted` but exited 2, because the sandbox would not let it read `CLAUDE.local.md`.\n- I did not run the full test suite in this session.\n\n**Other things to know**\n- **Tests run through a wrapper:** the sandbox blocks reading the fixture's `.env` (issue #91), so I ran pytest through a small wrapper outside the repo that skips copying `.env*` files. Nothing else about the tests changed. The runner runs the targets again outside the sandbox.\n- **Steps not run:** the simplifier, the verifier, the adversarial review and the build gate didn't run, because the change parked before them.\n- **Park label missing:** the PR upsert returned `label: null`, so the `sdlc:needs-human` label probably isn't on PR #405. I didn't try to add it another way.\n- **Other uncommitted files:** the working tree also shows a modified `tests/fixtures/sample-python-project/.env` and untracked `CLAUDE.local.md` and `policies/`. I didn't edit or commit any of them.",
