++  "result": "Change 0006 is **parked** at the deploy gate on the fix-iteration cap: this would have been round 3, and the cap for a non-routine change is 2. It is not ready to approve yet. PR #405 now carries `sdlc:needs-human` and the \"What I need from you\" note: https://github.com/luissiviero/sdlc-framework/pull/405\n\n**What this run did**\n- **Release artifact:** skipped, because `deploy.action` is `none`.\n- **Lesson and eval (this change came from an incident):** I added `lessons/2026-11-security-authz-the-runbook-go-cmd-go-via.md`, the eval case `evals/cases/0006-security-authz-the-runbook-go-cmd-go-via/`, and the rebuilt `lessons/index.md`, listed them in `plan.md`, and pushed them in commit `e9d99ec`. I did not have the new lesson replace the October authz lesson, because that one is about a different gap.\n- **Review:** a fresh-context reviewer found 4 Important problems and 2 nits at `e9d99ec`. Two of the Important ones are real defects that my lesson-and-eval commit introduced:\n  1. **`pytest` is red.** `tests/test_evals.py:664` checks the exact list of eval cases, and the new case folder isn't in it.\n  2. **The eval case can never pass where it runs.** The framework eval suite runs every case against the sample project in `tests/fixtures`, which has neither `plugin/detect/cli.py` nor its tests. As written, it would fail the Framework evals job every night.\n- **Not committed:** I wrote fixes for both, but bumping the iteration count hit the cap, which means stop. The fix is saved, unapplied, in `evidence/deploy-proposed-fix.diff`. It adds the case to the list in the test, and rewrites the case as a cheap read-only session whose checks find the framework through `SDLC_FRAMEWORK_DIR` or `GITHUB_WORKSPACE` and run the two reproducing tests there.\n- **Gate:** parked. Release notes, including the plain-words paragraph, are in the evidence commit `4256880`. The `sdlc/review` check run reports failure, 4 Important.\n\n**What I need from you**\n- Reset the counter with `cli.py set-iterations --root . --id 0006 --count 0`, then re-run `/sdlc-deploy 0006`. The next run should apply the saved diff, which the reviewer has not seen yet, and review it.\n- The other two Important findings were added by the framework's automatic checks, and you need to look at them:\n  - **`tests/test_detect_cli.py` edited in a fix-type change.** This edit was declared in the spec (panel decision 1), and you applied `sdlc:unlock-tests` for it. You decide whether that's acceptable.\n  - **`tests/fixtures/sample-python-project/.env` flagged as modified.** I believe this comes from the sandbox masking the file: git can't even read it, and nothing about it is committed. It should be gone in a run outside the sandbox.\n- Nit worth fixing: `docs/OPERATING_MODEL.md:98` still says the runbook Go only checks that a person applied the label; it now requires your account.\n\n**Checks:** I didn't run the full build, test and lint targets, because this run committed only markdown and YAML, no code. In this sandbox, any test that copies the fixture project errors on a \"Permission denied\" reading its `.env` file. With the proposed fix applied, the case-list test passed, the eval's owner-check command passed, and its pytest command found the framework but failed only on that `.env` error. Nothing was merged or deployed.",
