++  "result": "## Review of change 0006: no Important findings, 2 nits\n\nI found nothing that blocks this change. I wrote the findings to `changes/0006-security-authz-the-runbook-go-cmd-go-via/evidence/review-findings.json` and the security brief to `evidence/roles/security-policy-deploy.md`. I did not run the tests myself; the evidence logs show the build, all tests (2888 passed, 1 skipped) and lint green. The `at` time in the findings file is approximate, set by hand.\n\n**The fix itself:** `_human_label_actor` now refuses a `sdlc:go` label unless `is_owner_actor` says it came from the owner's account. It checks after the existing bot/automation refusal and before the runbook proposal is judged. The owner is read from the default branch's copy of `sdlc.yaml`, not the pull request's copy. One test covers a collaborator applying the label. A second covers `owner:` named only in the pull request's copy (still refused) and named on `main` (that account's label runs the runbook).\n\n**Nits:**\n1. `tests/test_detect_cli.py:351` \u2014 This is a fix-type change, and REVIEW.md says such a change must not edit test files that already existed. This one adds one line to the `rollback_incident` fixture and adds the new tests to that same file. I rated it a nit, not Important, because:\n   - the spec declares the fixture edit (panel decision 1);\n   - it went in with the reproducing test, before the test files were locked;\n   - no existing test's body or assertion changed.\n\n   Read literally, the rule still forbids it, so please confirm which reading you want.\n2. `docs/OPERATING_MODEL.md:98` \u2014 the `sdlc-runbook.yml` row still says the Go step only checks that the label came from a person. It now also requires the owner's account, so the doc understates the check.\n\n**Plan conformance:** the diff follows `plan.md`: only the two planned files changed, in the planned order. The one change made during a fix round (what the collaborator test asserts) updated `plan.md` in the same commit.\n\n**Risk item `auth`:** my verdict is continue. The change tightens who can trigger a runbook. If no account other than the owner's applies the label, nothing runs. An organization repository that doesn't set `owner:` in `sdlc.yaml` will refuse every Go until it does. To undo it, revert commit `6a2429f` together with the two new tests.",
