++++  "result": "The fix for change 0006 is committed, but the build is **parked**: one of the reproducing tests is itself wrong, and the test files are locked. Draft PR: https://github.com/luissiviero/sdlc-framework/pull/405\n\n**What was done on `sdlc/0006/build`**\n1. `5ae9227` \u2014 the reproducing tests. I added the fixture line that names `the-owner` as the owner (panel decision 1) and the two new tests. With the fixture line alone, all 96 tests in `tests/test_detect_cli.py` passed. The three new cases then failed with `performed` True, which is the weakness the intent describes. The log is in `evidence/failing-test.log`. After this commit the test files were locked.\n2. `6a2429f` \u2014 the fix. `_human_label_actor` in `plugin/detect/cli.py` now refuses a `sdlc:go` label that wasn't applied by the owner's account. It uses `is_owner_actor` with the default branch's `sdlc.yaml`, imported at the top of the module.\n3. Park commit, then the PR number recorded, both pushed.\n\n**Why it's parked**\n`tests/test_detect_cli.py:859` in `test_go_by_a_collaborator_performs_nothing` asserts `runbook_records(change) == []`. I copied that line from plan.md step 1, but it can never pass: the test's own `dispatch` step writes `evidence/runbook-rollback-deploy.json` with status `go-requested`. The existing `test_dispatch_go_route_records_go_requested_and_runs_nothing` asserts the same file. After the fix, everything else in that test passes: nothing runs, no label changes, the reason names the owner and the colleague, and `runbook_authorized_by` stays null.\n\n**What I need from you**\n| File | Row | Now | Must become |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [tests/test_detect_cli.py](tests/test_detect_cli.py#L859) | 859 | `assert runbook_records(change) == []` | `record = json.loads((change / \"evidence\" / \"runbook-rollback-deploy.json\").read_text(\"utf-8\"))` then `assert record[\"status\"] == \"go-requested\"` |\n\nThe tests have to be unlocked first. Then re-run `/sdlc-build 0006`.\n\n